      "problem": "${\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{3}{1+{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})\\text{d}t=$",
      "worked_solution": "We split the integral into the sum of two integrals and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{3}{1+{t}^{2}}+{t}^{2})\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{arctan}⁡t\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0)+\\frac{1}{3}({1}^{3}-{0}^{1}) \\\\  & =3(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0)+\\frac{1}{3}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi +4}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
